 - Writes require the `contributor` or `manager` role in the project. Users who can read but not write get 403.
 - Contributors may only modify tasks assigned to themselves, and may not reassign tasks. Managers may modify any task.
 - Only managers may delete tasks.
+- Moving a task (`.../move`) takes the task out of its project, so it needs the manager role in the source project (else 403). The destination must be readable by the user (else 404), must accept writes for the user (contributor or manager there, else 403), and must not be archived (else 409). Moving to the task's current project → 400.
+- A move keeps the task's ID, title, status and assignee. The assignee must be a contributor or manager of the destination (else 400). A contributor in the destination may only keep a task assigned to themselves (else 403).
 - Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
 
